<https://purl.org/arlem-onto#hasPoi> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Specify the point of interest (poi) from where to remove the\n            augmentation"@en .
# 
# https://purl.org/arlem-onto#hasPredicate
<https://purl.org/arlem-onto#hasPredicate> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://purl.org/arlem-onto#hasPredicate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://purl.org/arlem-onto#action> .
<https://purl.org/arlem-onto#hasPredicate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The action may specify what verb to log user interaction with\n            via the xAPI.\n            When no predicate is provided, logging shall use the standard xAPI verb “launched” for\n            each action step.\n            If xAPI is supported by the AR training system, then any predicate id used shall\n            correspond to the id of the resultant xAPI verb statement definition."@en .
# 
# https://purl.org/arlem-onto#hasPredicates
<https://purl.org/arlem-onto#hasPredicates> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://purl.org/arlem-onto#hasPredicates> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://purl.org/arlem-onto#workplace> .
<https://purl.org/arlem-onto#hasPredicates> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Predicates are reusable instructional augmentations, configuring\n            a specific augmentation primitive for its use in activities."@en .
# 
# https://purl.org/arlem-onto#hasPrimitives
<https://purl.org/arlem-onto#hasPrimitives> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://purl.org/arlem-onto#hasPrimitives> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://purl.org/arlem-onto#workplace> .
<https://purl.org/arlem-onto#hasPrimitives> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Augmentation primitives define the fundamental types of\n            annotations available in the AR training system\n            NOTE—The workplace model informs the AR training system, which of the primitives are\n            supported in this workplace. Moreover, for each augmentation primitive, the workplace\n            model defines default size and/or volume level."@en .
